.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-HOOK" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-hook - Load ENV in plain ssh and VS Code shells through a shell startup hook


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env hook [bash|zsh|fish] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Without flags, print the hook line for a shell. --install adds that line to the shell's startup file (~/.bashrc, ~/.zshenv or ~/.config/fish/config.fish) for the account logged in here and the active workspace; --uninstall removes it. VS Code Remote-SSH: after installing, run "Remote-SSH: Kill VS Code Server on Host" and reconnect.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for hook

.PP
\fB--install\fP[=false]
	add the hook line to the shell startup file and record the account and workspace

.PP
\fB--status\fP[=false]
	show whether the hook is installed and whose ENV it loads

.PP
\fB--uninstall\fP[=false]
	remove the hook line from every shell startup file and forget the recorded choice


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
